lesson: 140
title: Ages that grow together: sum and difference
level: primary-2
stars: 3
explain: Each year both children get one year older, so the sum of two ages grows by 2 each year, and the difference never changes.
explain: If two ages add up to 20 and one child is 4 years older, the younger is (20 − 4) ÷ 2 = 8.
explain: If in 3 years the two ages will add up to 26, today they add up to 26 − 3 − 3 = 20.
vars: a=name b=name x=6..14 d=2..6 n=2..5
let: s = 2 * x + d
answer: x
exercise: {a} and {b} are together {s} years old now. {b} is {d} years older than {a}. How old is {a}?
exercise: In {n} years the ages of {a} and {b} will add up to {s+2*n}. {b} is {d} years older than {a}. How old is {a} now?
exercise: {n} years ago {a} and {b} were {s-2*n} years old together. {b} is {d} years older. How old is {a} now?
exercise: In {n} years {b} will be {d} years older than {a}, and together they will be {s+2*n}. How old is {a} today?
exercise: {n} years ago {b} was {x+d-n} years old. {b} is {d} years older than {a}. How old is {a} now?
exercise: The sum of the ages of {a} and {b} in {n} years will be {s+2*n}. Now {b} is {x+d}. How old is {a} now?
test: Today {b} is older than {a} by {d} years. {n} years from now the two of them will be {s+2*n} years old together. What is {a}'s age today?
test: {s-2*n} was the total of {a}'s and {b}'s ages {n} years ago, and {b} is the elder by {d} years. Find {a}'s present age.
test: {a} and {b} differ in age by {d} years. In {n} years the sum of their ages will be {s+2*n}. How many years old is the younger one now?
test: In {n} years {a} and {b} will be {s+2*n} years old together, and {b} will then be {x+d+n}. How old is {a} now?
exercise: How old is {a}, if {a} and {b} are {s} years old together and {b} is {d} years older?
exercise: Ages now: sum {s}, {b} older by {d}. How old is {a}?
exercise: {a} and {b} live in Ohio. Their ages add up to {s} today, and {a} is {d} years younger than {b}. How old is {a}?
exercise: In {n.words} years, {a}'s age plus {b}'s age will be {s+2*n}. {b} is {d.words} years older than {a}. How old is {a} now?
exercise: {n} years ago the ages of {a} and {b} added up to {s-2*n}. {a} is {d} years younger than {b}. What is {a}'s age now?
exercise: {b} is {x+d} today. In {n} years the ages of {a} and {b} combined will be {s+2*n}. How old is {a} today?
exercise: Two cousins from Leeds, {a} and {b}, are {d} years apart, {b} being the older. Their ages now make {s} in total. How old is {a}?
exercise: {b} will be {x+d+n} in {n} years. {a} is {d} years younger than {b}. How old is {a} now?
test: In Sydney, {a} is younger than {b} by {d} years, and their ages together come to {s}. Find {a}'s age.
test: {n} years from now, {a} and {b} will be {s+2*n} years old combined. {b} is the older, by {d} years. How old is {a} at present?
test: Back {n} years, {b} was {x+d-n}. {a} is {d} years younger than {b}. How many years old is {a} now?
test: What is the age of the younger of two friends from Toronto, if their ages add up to {s} and one is {d} years older?
test: {s-2*n} years: that was the total age of {a} and {b} {n} years ago. If {a} is {d} years younger, how old is {a} now?
test: {b} turns {x+d+n} in {n} years. Today the sum of {a}'s and {b}'s ages is {s}. How old is {a}?
exercise: {a} n {b} are {s} together, {b}'s {d} older. how old's {a}
exercise: {a} and {b} add up to {s+1} years — no wait, {s}. {b} is {d} years older. {a}'s age?
exercise: my cousin says if they're {s} together and {b}'s {d} older then {a} is {s-d}. nah. how old is {a} really
exercise: in {n} years {a} and {b} will be {s+2*n} together, {b}'s {d} years older, got a dog thats 3. how old is {a} now
test: {b} is {d} years older than {a}, both together {s}. {a}'s how old
test: together {a} n {b} = {s} years. {b} older by {d}. {a}?
test: {a} reckons {a.he}'s {x+d}, cos {a.he} and {b} make {s} and {b}'s {d} older. wrong innit? how old is {a}
exam: It is given that the combined present ages of {a} and {b} amount to {s} years and that {b} is the elder by {d} years. Determine the present age of {a}.
exam: Whereas in {n} years' time the ages of {a} and {b} will total {s+2*n} years, and {b} is {d} years the elder, ascertain the present age of {a}.
exam: {n.words} years ago the ages of {a} and {b} totalled {s-2*n} years; {b} is {d} years older than {a}. State the present age of {a} in years.
exam: Compute the lesser of two whole numbers whose sum is {s} and whose difference is {d}.
exercise: {a} bends the truth about {a.his} age: {a.he} says {a.he} is as old as {b}. Really {b} is {d} years older, and together they are {s}. How old is {a} really?
exercise: Grandad passed away {n} years ago. Back then {a} and {b} were {s-2*n} years old together, and {b} is {d} years older than {a}. How old is {a} now?
test: {b} was economical with the truth again, "I'm the baby". rubbish. {b}'s {d} years older than {a} and together they're {s}. so how old's {a}, genius?
